// FORBID-polarity guardrail under the same three-action list scope. Deny
// Read/Write/Delete when the document name is long. Because forbid
// overrides permit, the out-of-scope Ping with a long document is the
// discriminating timepoint: if this forbid's scope leaked to Ping, the
// Ping verdict would flip to false — unlike the permit-polarity variant
// (case 5000), where an extra permit masks a scope leak.
forbid (
    principal,
    action in [Drupe::Action::"Read", Drupe::Action::"Write", Drupe::Action::"Delete"],
    resource
)
when guardrails {
    Strings::Length(context.input.document).length >= 6
};
